ligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =1+3 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =4 \\\\ R & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266545 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266546 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266547 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266548 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266549 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1041 "selection" 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266548 13194139533930 true] [17592186266544 1110 #uuid "dc53fca3-abf7-574e-8d39-b66758efc0b4" 13194139533930 true] [17592186266545 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533930 true] [17592186266545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533930 true] [17592186266545 1111 #uuid "d2fbe32d-2471-5f31-8937-5a976a